I often find myself without either an athame or a magic marker needing to 
engrave Elbereth. As I am loathe to destroy the edge on my favourite
plus-whatever weapon I try to use whatever other sharp object is to hand, 
usually an orcish dagger. Unfortunately an orcish dagger doesn't quite have
what it takes - engraving wise - it'll get you to 'Elberet` but that is all.

What I want to know is, why can't I finish off the engraving with another 
dagger. If you try to engrave again it tells you that there is already
something written there and that you cannot erase it. Since all I want to do
is add an `h' on the end, I find this rather frustrating. Couldn't the message
tell you that there is already something written there and ask you if you 
want to add anything to it? For example see the following - 

there is already something written here - you see `Elberet' -more- 
do you want to add to this? [y/n]
what do you wish to append?

I lost a very good character this way once. I was cornered by a ghost and 
engraved Elbereth, however I foolishly used an orcish dagger. Although I
had a huge stack of sharp objects with which to write, my goose was cooked as
I couldn't find any way to add on the `h'.

